  official in charge of the nicaraguan  mission which brought about soldier  boy's death in the 80s the u.s  government and payback worked together  to sell cocaine in order to finance the  government's war against the  russian-backed sandinistas the whole  mission was a failure with soldier boy's  dead body picked up by the russians we  do know soldier boy is alive from the  previews and judging by the carnage he  gets up to i wonder if there's a whole  winter soldier type thing going on here  where soldier boy was revived and  brainwashed by the russians or this  could totally be a ruse we never really  see what happened to soldier boy and the  person we get this info from is soldier  boy's girlfriend the crimson countess  who by the way is a washed up superhero  who performs for small near-empty crowds  at an amusement park although her hit  song chimps don't cry is a banger you  know the chimps are physically incapable  of crying the operation in nicaragua  also known as operation charlie is based  off a real operation in south america in  which the united states backed  right-wing dictatorships it's here we  get our first look at young stan edgar  in charge of managing the payback team  he's hoping to prove that supes can be  used in the military something that even  in the present day hasn't been approved  now huey investigates red river where he  sees this boy named teddy stillwell  which was the name of madeleine  stillwell's infant son in season one  with his mother dead at the hands or  should i say eyes of homelander it looks  like this is where he ended up it's by  grabbing red river's files that huey  learns not only about victoria newman's  past it looks as though she may have  killed her parents or others as a child  bonus points if he caught the gal gear  adds in the back of the vaught rifle  association which was seen on vnn or  gunpowder's second amendment forever  license plate butcher ends up viciously  killing gunpowder but i also got the  vibe 