  raised without a father figure maybe  butcher needs to learn to fulfill that  role not only for ryan's good but for  himself we'll also see ryan drop his  necklace of saint christopher a present  given to him by butcher at the end of  season 2. the legend of saint  christopher tells the story of a man who  helped a small child across a river only  for it to be revealed that the child is  christ so this is symbolic of butcher  turning away from being that person if  ryan is to be this christ-like figure  frenchie goes on a mission of his own  when he finds out his good friend sherry  is on the run for stealing from the  russian mob particularly a woman named  little nina in the comics she is  depicted as extremely short with an  affinity for vibrators and is later  killed when butcher plants an explosive  in one of them this may tie into the  action from one of the trailers which  shows kimiko using dildos as weapons in  an absolutely disgusting scene where the  deep has to eat his own octopus and  friend named timothy homelander compares  his struggle to that of martin luther  king hilarious considering he loved a  white supremacist and hates any sort of  marginalized group captain al qaeda  we're americans but this all seems to be  leading to homelander becoming more and  more powerful narcissistic and unruly so  it's all becoming a race against time  for the boys to find a way to stop him  once and for all butcher says he'll use  little nina as their way into russia  maybe she'll have information about  soldier boy's whereabouts we do know  that butcher kimiko and frenchie will  make it to wherever soldier boy has been  hiding by the looks of it in some sort  of cryostasis i'm really looking forward  to when soldier boy is finally released  and homelander will truly have someone  to rival him thanks a lot for watching  everyone be sure to like and subscribe  and let me know your thoughts and  theories for episodes one to three for  more bad takes you can always 